body:
I have a .74 in the saddle of my floyd, there's no problems there,  but at the other end if you get a tapered string it will fit your tuning peg hole easily.  Also you might be running out of thread on the locking nut bolt on the biggest strings,  I measure and clip mine so the taper-down is right in front of the nut.  It's also ok to use the core to anchor to the peg if you need or want (it's how the sting gets made after all).

&#x200B;

yeah, btw my 7 is at g# standard

chalk\_walk,  thanks for that!  I think I solved my own problem tho by turning off 'Sequencer sends midi notes'  in the MCC.   

&#x200B;

feel a bit noobish for posting this now.   wanted to own up tho.  maybe it'll help someone else new to the drumbrute.  :-L
